Host-side regression harness for the HP-over-cap bug flagged in review at
commit ad370e9: a +maxHp sponsor from the previous floor could leave hp
above the new floor's effective cap once that sponsor rolled off, letting
the HUD show e.g. "HP: 22 / 20". Not a gtest suite (see test/README for
those) -- this compiles the REAL, unmodified GameActivity.cpp (specifically
its private loadOrGenerateLevel(), exercised only through the real public
onEnter() entry point) against the REAL GfxRenderer/EpdFont/DungeonGenerator/
GameState/GameSave/AchievementBus/FlavorText pipeline, so the clamp is
proven against shipped code, not a transcription of it.

Same standalone-g++, symlinked-mirror-with-shadow-headers technique as
test/game_title_render/ -- see that README's "Why mirror/ exists" section
for the general explanation. This harness needed two additional shadow
headers beyond that precedent (test/sponsor_hp_clamp/stubs/
MappedInputManager.h, test/sponsor_hp_clamp/stubs_settings/
CrossPointSettings.h) because GameActivity.cpp pulls in a wider dependency
surface than GameTitleActivity.cpp did -- see the comment at the top of each
stub for exactly why the real header wasn't usable and why the stub is
correct rather than a workaround-in-hiding.

## Why loadOrGenerateLevel() is reachable at all

It's private. It's called unconditionally, exactly once, from the real
public GameActivity::onEnter() (GameActivity.cpp:98-114) -- the only public
entry point that reaches it. Real gameplay floor transitions instead go
through render()'s StairsDown/StairsUp branches, which would require
simulating RenderLock/movement and isn't worth it here: the harness instead
runs many independent trials, each via GAME_STATE.newGame() + a fresh
GameActivity + onEnter(), and inspects whatever sponsor onEnter() actually
rolled and whether hp survived clamped.

## Build

  INCLUDES="-include Arduino.h \
    -I test/sponsor_hp_clamp/stubs_settings \
    -I test/sponsor_hp_clamp/stubs \
    -I test/sponsor_hp_clamp/mirror/src \
    -I test/sponsor_hp_clamp/mirror/src/activities \
    -I test/sponsor_hp_clamp/mirror/src/activities/game \
    -I src -I src/game \
    -I lib/EpdFont/builtinFonts -I lib/EpdFont -I lib/Epub -I lib/FsHelpers \
    -I lib/GfxRenderer -I lib/I18n -I lib/InflateReader -I lib/JpegToBmpConverter \
    -I lib/JsonParser -I lib/KOReaderSync -I lib/Logging -I lib/Memory \
    -I lib/MiniBidi -I lib/OpdsParser -I lib/Serialization -I lib/Txt -I lib/Utf8 \
    -I lib/XmlParserUtils -I lib/Xtc -I lib/ZipFile -I lib/expat -I lib/hal \
    -I lib/miniz -I lib/uzlib -I lib/uzlib/src \
    -I /home/skippy/build/crosspoint-llama-pro/.pio/libdeps/x4pro/ArduinoJson/src"

Two real prerequisites, not stubs -- run once if missing:
  - I18n codegen (needed by GameRenderer.cpp's #include "I18nKeys.h"):
      python3 scripts/gen_i18n.py
  - ArduinoJson (real vendored dep per platformio.ini:99, reused from the
    old non-git ~/build/crosspoint-llama-pro/.pio/libdeps/x4pro cache --
    not re-vendored, not faked).

  mkdir -p /tmp/objs2
  for src in \
      test/sponsor_hp_clamp/SponsorHpClampHarness.cpp \
      test/sponsor_hp_clamp/mirror/src/activities/game/GameActivity.cpp \
      test/sponsor_hp_clamp/mirror/src/activities/Activity.cpp \
      src/game/AchievementBus.cpp \
      src/game/DungeonGenerator.cpp \
      src/game/FlavorText.cpp \
      src/game/GameRenderer.cpp \
      src/game/GameSave.cpp \
      src/game/GameSprites.cpp \
      src/game/GameState.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/GfxRenderer.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/Bitmap.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/BitmapHelpers.cpp \
      lib/GfxRenderer/FontCacheManager.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/EpdFont.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/EpdFontFamily.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/FontDecompressor.cpp \
      lib/EpdFont/SdCardFont.cpp \
      lib/InflateReader/InflateReader.cpp \
      lib/Utf8/Utf8.cpp \
      lib/MiniBidi/BidiUtils.cpp \
      lib/Memory/BuildScratch.cpp \
      lib/I18n/I18n.cpp \
      lib/I18n/I18nStrings.cpp \
      ; do
    obj=/tmp/objs2/$(basename "${src%.*}" | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z').o
    g++ -std=c++20 -O2 -Wall -Wextra $INCLUDES -c "$src" -o "$obj"
  done

  # Plain C, not C++ -- same reasons as test/game_title_render/README:
  gcc -O2 -I test/game_title_render/stubs -I lib/uzlib -I lib/uzlib/src \
    -c lib/uzlib/src/tinflate.c -o /tmp/objs2/tinflate.o
  gcc -O2 -I test/game_title_render/stubs -I lib/uzlib -I lib/uzlib/src \
    -c test/game_title_render/stubs/uzlib_checksum_stub.c -o /tmp/objs2/uzlib_checksum_stub.o
  gcc -O2 -I lib/MiniBidi -c lib/MiniBidi/minibidi.c -o /tmp/objs2/minibidi.o

  g++ /tmp/objs2/*.o -o /tmp/sponsor_hp_clamp_harness

## Run

  /tmp/sponsor_hp_clamp_harness

Prints one summary line ("[sponsor-hp-clamp] N trials ... M/N rolled a
different sponsor, K clamp violations (worst overage X hp)") plus
"ALL CHECKS PASSED" or "K CHECK(S) FAILED", exit code 0/1.

## Shadow headers used, and exactly why each is scoped-safe

- stubs/MappedInputManager.h: GameActivity.cpp's own calls (wasReleased,
  wasScreenTapped) are never reached by the onEnter()-only call path, but
  GameRenderer.h references MappedInputManager::Button/SwipeDir/etc. in
  unused method signatures, so the full real type surface must exist even
  though nothing calls it. All bodies are inert no-ops.
- stubs_settings/CrossPointSettings.h: only referenced from
  GameRenderer::draw() (SETTINGS.gameTheme, SETTINGS.getRefreshFrequency()),
  never called by this harness since it never invokes render()/draw(). Real
  CrossPointSettings pulls in a hardware-coupled BoardConfig.h chain
  (freeink-sdk symlink) inappropriate for a host harness -- unlike
  ArduinoJson, which is a genuine reusable dependency and is NOT stubbed.
- mirror/src/activities/game/GameMenuActivity.h: same pattern, pre-existing
  from before this harness -- GameActivity holds one as a sibling activity
  but this harness's onEnter()-only path never transitions into it.

## Why mirror/ exists

Same as test/game_title_render/README: mirror/src/... are symlinks back to
the real src/... tree, not copies, so GameActivity.cpp and Activity.cpp
compile byte-identical to shipped source. Only the two headers above are
real shadow stubs, both justified above by call-path analysis, not
convenience.
